PROJECT: Complete Varek → Cole Rebrand and Minimalist UI/UX Redesign

1. Your Role and Mission

You are a senior product designer, UI/UX architect, frontend engineer, and brand identity specialist.

Your assignment is to completely transform the existing application Varek into Cole, a sophisticated, minimalist, monochromatic browser-local intelligence assistant.

This is a comprehensive product rebrand and interface redesign, not a superficial color replacement.

You must work directly within the existing repository, understand its architecture, modify the implementation, and deliver a cohesive, production-ready result.

Repository: https://github.com/hiyroscript/varek

New product name: Cole

Core aesthetic: Premium minimalism, editorial sophistication, quiet confidence, architectural simplicity, and monochromatic precision.

Primary objectives

1. Completely replace the Varek visual identity with Cole.
2. Replace the current cream, mauve, and purple color scheme with a strictly black, white, and grayscale design system.
3. Redesign the entire user interface to feel exceptionally clean, simple, organized, spacious, and modern.
4. Improve information hierarchy, layout composition, typography, interactions, responsiveness, and visual consistency.
5. Create a new minimalist Cole logo and complete accompanying icon system.
6. Ensure the website, PWA, and Chromium extension share one cohesive identity.
7. Preserve all existing functionality, storage, security, offline capabilities, and assistant behavior.
8. Deliver actual implementation changes, not mockups, suggestions, or a high-level design proposal.

Do not stop after planning. Audit the codebase, implement the redesign, run validation, fix regressions, and report the finished work.

