19. Preserve User Data and Backward Compatibility

This is a mandatory requirement.

The existing application stores conversations in the IndexedDB database named varek.

Preferences are stored under the local-storage key varek.preferences.v1.

The offline service worker also uses Varek-related cache identifiers.

Do not casually rename these internal identifiers.

Aesthetic rebranding must never cause users to lose saved conversations, settings, pinned chats, or cached data.

Preferred approach

Preserve legacy persistence identifiers internally where necessary for backward compatibility.

If changing internal storage names is genuinely beneficial, implement a carefully designed, tested migration with backup-safe behavior and no destructive automatic reset.

A visible Cole identity is more important than eliminating every historical internal identifier.

Existing user data must remain available after upgrading.

Preserve existing conversation data, model metadata, personalization, and saved preferences.

Do not rewrite user-authored conversation text merely because it contains the old product name.

Retain necessary legacy compatibility mappings, including historical Zulvyn model migration behavior.

Cache handling

Review the current service worker cache naming and cleanup logic carefully.

Ensure older Varek application-shell caches can be upgraded or retired safely without deleting unrelated caches or model data.

Avoid premature service worker registration changes that could break offline operation.

Preserve current extension-origin storage behavior.

Branding audit

Expand scripts/check-brand.ts as appropriate.

Detect unexpected visible Varek branding in product surfaces while explicitly allowlisting legitimate compatibility identifiers, historical fixtures, existing deployment URLs, and migration logic.

Do not break the existing Zulvyn legacy-brand audit.

